> How do you decide what a game goal is?

I'm on the line of the poster who said the only goal is Ascension.
(Personally I have "subgoals" - better called *milestones* -, like
getting the basic resistances, getting a unicorn horn, etc.)

But Nethack is a complex game, and people often don't manage ascend
even after playing years. So I think it's a valid view to say that
"The Way [to Ascension] is the Goal.", which is somewhat subjective
(and may include objectively "suboptimal" playing styles) and thus
not appropriate as a "game goal".

